   only-main: It is printed here, read when the set stood at eleven.
   only-PP:   It is printed here, read on the current eleven.
   only-PP:   E(G), recomputed by the press at every build, across the six fibres of F.2 and on the coordinates as now constrained — 38 as first
   only-PP:   stated, 24 once register 367's constraint is imposed, and 23 after §12.11.0.1's four-cap table
   only-PP:   occupied one. Each remaining cell is a combination of definition, inputs and verification admitted by
   only-PP:   the structure of what the book prints and occupied by nothing it prints.
   only-PP:   And seventeen of the twenty-three are cells the book should not want. Each admitted cell was
   only-PP:   tested against the cells its own fibre already occupies:
   only-PP:   standing cells
   only-PP:   dominated — some occupied cell of that fibre is at least as good on all three axes 17
   only-PP:   not dominated — genuinely above what the fibre already carries 6
   only-PP:   A dominated cell is a weaker description of a number than the fibre already achieves: a bound
   only-PP:   recomputed but with its definition merely asserted, where the fibre already holds bounds stated with
   only-PP:   their inputs. Occupying it would mean writing a worse paragraph.
   only-PP:   E(X) counts what a structure admits without asking whether occupying it is an improvement.
   only-PP:   On an ordered index the admitted-and-absent set contains cells below the object's own practice
   only-PP:   as readily as above it, and only the second kind is work.
   only-PP:   That is a third resolution §12's loop does not offer. The loop gives two — a cell is filled by a
   only-PP:   number that belongs there, or excluded by a constraint the coordinates are missing. Seventeen of these
   only-PP:   are neither: admitted, unoccupied, and correctly so. The actionable count for this index is six,
   only-PP:   and five of the six are verification = under variation, which is one computation each at several cap
   only-PP:   settings rather than a search or a judgement. Register 368.
