   §2.16.1 body (E.4 L11126 *what §2.16.1 claims for it*):
   L729 ### 2.16.1 Why this is the method and not a technique
   L730  It is Chapter 6 applied to the book's own ignorance. A periodic table with 36 unfilled cells does not
   L731  need a chemist to guess which are missing — the layout shows them. An open question with eight
   L732  unfilled requirements does not need twenty-two attempts — the grid shows that four of them are one.
   L734  Worked on §30.3: eight empty cells, four rows deep, at d ≥ 3.
   L736   requirement                     d=2                                d≥3
   L737   characterisation                proved                             ·
   L738   decision procedure              linear                             ·
   L739   YES certificate                 an order                           an order
   L740   NO certificate                  Tucker — unbounded                 unbounded
   L741   obstruction family              Tucker 1972                        unbounded, route closed
   L742   construction rules              six preserving                     six preserving
   L743   hardness                        P, the CSP is binary               ·
   L744   the data structure              PQ-tree                            ·
   L746     Three rows are full at every d, and they are the three that needed no d-specific work —
   L747     the certificate is the order itself, the obstruction family is Tucker's, the construction rules were
   L748     established once. Every empty cell is downstream of one missing object: the d ≥ 3 analogue
   L749     of a PQ-tree.
   L751  Twenty-two formulations were attempts on four cells that depend on one. The grid says so in
   L752  a table; hunting concealed it for a day.
